@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-repeal`

-- ca-tests-repeal.l4
--
-- What a repeal does: sections 2(2), 39(2), 43, 44 and 46.
-- Expected values written from the text before the module was run.

§ `Section 2(2): treated as repealed`

#ASSERT NOT (`for the purposes of the Act, an enactment is treated as repealed if` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE)
#ASSERT `for the purposes of the Act, an enactment is treated as repealed if` TRUE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `for the purposes of the Act, an enactment is treated as repealed if` FALSE `or` TRUE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `for the purposes of the Act, an enactment is treated as repealed if` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` TRUE

§ `Section 39(2): a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on 2026-06-10`

-- Before the day: the regulation is in force, the law it revoked or amended is not.  After the day: the reverse.
#ASSERT `a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 11))
#ASSERT NOT (`a law revoked or amended by the making of a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force in its earlier form on` (YMD 2026 6 9))
#ASSERT `a law revoked or amended by the making of a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force in its earlier form on` (YMD 2026 6 11)
-- On the day of the resolution itself the text gives the day, not the moment: a refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 10))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a law revoked or amended by the making of a regulation annulled by a resolution passed on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `is in force in its earlier form on` (YMD 2026 6 10))
-- The validity of what was done in compliance is not affected.
#ASSERT `an action taken or not taken in compliance with the annulled regulation is valid after the resolution if it was` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an action taken or not taken in compliance with the annulled regulation is valid after the resolution if it was` FALSE)

§ `Section 43: what a repeal does to each thing`

#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `an enactment, or anything, not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` EQUALS `the repeal does not revive it`
#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `the previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it` EQUALS `the repeal does not affect it`
#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` EQUALS `the repeal does not affect it`
#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `an offence against, or a contravention of the provisions of, the repealed enactment` EQUALS `the repeal does not affect it`
#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `a punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the repealed enactment` EQUALS `the repeal does not affect it`
#ASSERT `what section 43 says the repeal does to` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability, or of such a punishment, penalty or forfeiture` EQUALS `the repeal does not affect it`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`what section 43 says the repeal does to` `anything else`)
-- The closing words: an investigation, proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and a punishment imposed, as if not repealed.
#ASSERT `it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability, or of such a punishment, penalty or forfeiture`
#ASSERT `it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` `a punishment, penalty or forfeiture incurred under the repealed enactment`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` `an offence against, or a contravention of the provisions of, the repealed enactment`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`it may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed, if it is` `anything else`)

§ `Section 44: repeal and substitution`

-- (a)
#ASSERT `a person who was acting under the former enactment continues to act under the new enactment if` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person who was acting under the former enactment continues to act under the new enactment if` TRUE)
-- (b)
#ASSERT `a bond or security remains in force if` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a bond or security remains in force if` FALSE)
#ASSERT `books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment continue to be used as before the repeal if` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`books, papers, forms and things made or used under the former enactment continue to be used as before the repeal if` FALSE)
-- (c)
#ASSERT `a proceeding taken under the former enactment is taken up and continued under the new enactment if` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proceeding taken under the former enactment is taken up and continued under the new enactment if` FALSE)
-- (d)
#ASSERT `the procedure of the new enactment is followed in recovering fines, enforcing rights or proceeding on earlier matters if` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the procedure of the new enactment is followed in recovering fines, enforcing rights or proceeding on earlier matters if` FALSE)
-- (e): reduced by the new enactment AND imposed after the repeal.
#ASSERT `the punishment, penalty or forfeiture that applies where` TRUE `and` TRUE EQUALS `the punishment as reduced or mitigated by the new enactment`
#ASSERT `the punishment, penalty or forfeiture that applies where` TRUE `and` FALSE EQUALS `the punishment under the former enactment`
#ASSERT `the punishment, penalty or forfeiture that applies where` FALSE `and` TRUE EQUALS `the punishment under the former enactment`
#ASSERT `the punishment, penalty or forfeiture that applies where` FALSE `and` FALSE EQUALS `the punishment under the former enactment`
-- (f)
#ASSERT `the new enactment's provision is read, if` TRUE EQUALS `as a consolidation and as declaratory of the law in the former enactment`
#ASSERT `the new enactment's provision is read, if` FALSE EQUALS `as capable of operating as new law, to the extent that it is not in substance the same`
-- (g): a regulation not inconsistent remains in force until repealed or others made; one that is inconsistent is not addressed.
#ASSERT `a regulation made under the repealed enactment remains in force as made under the new enactment if` FALSE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a regulation made under the repealed enactment remains in force as made under the new enactment if` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a regulation made under the repealed enactment remains in force as made under the new enactment if` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a regulation made under the repealed enactment remains in force as made under the new enactment if` TRUE `and` TRUE)
-- (h): a reference in an unrepealed enactment.
#ASSERT `a reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment is read, where` TRUE `and` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the provisions of the new enactment on the same subject-matter`
#ASSERT `a reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment is read, where` TRUE `and` FALSE EQUALS `as a reference to the former enactment read as unrepealed in so far as is necessary to maintain or give effect to the unrepealed enactment`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment is read, where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a reference in an unrepealed enactment to the former enactment is read, where` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `Section 46: demise of the Crown`

#ASSERT NOT (`a demise of the Crown affects` `the holding of an office under the Crown in right of Canada`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a demise of the Crown affects` `the need for the holder of such an office to be appointed again`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a demise of the Crown affects` `the need for the holder of such an office to take again an oath of office or allegiance already taken before the demise`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a demise of the Crown affects` `a writ, action or other process or proceeding, civil or criminal, in or issuing out of a court established by an Act`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a demise of the Crown affects` `anything else`)
